---
// website/src/pages/index.astro — the site's front page (website plan, Task W1.4; redesign
// parts P5 and P8; the owner's approved draft "Home, draft 2 (slider)", 2026-10-19).
//
// **The page is three blocks, and the draft says which three**: the hero — the title, the
// prompt line and the one-line promise, with the call to action the site has always had — then
// one slider whose three tabs are how it is to use, why it is worth it and what it looks like
// running, then one large "Get started" button with the install command under it. The page
// before this one was five blocks: the hero, the chat, the flow, the four benefits and two
// install cards. The draft folds the middle three into the slider's panels and the last two
// into the button, which is why this file renders `Hero`, `HomeSlider` and `HomeInstall` and
// nothing else.
//
// **What left the page, and where it went.** The chat's illustration is the slider's first
// panel in the draft's own words — the three steps a reader takes, each with a line of the
// README under it — so `AgentChat.astro` is gone rather than hidden: a component no page
// renders is a component whose build-time guards no longer run. The flow (`ArchitectureDiagram.astro`)
// is still on `/how-it-works/`, where the run's four steps have the room to be drawn; the
// benefits are still `Benefits.astro`, rendered by the slider's second panel; and the two
// install cards are the button above the one command most readers run, with every path still
// laid out on `/getting-started/`.
//
// Every block reads what it renders through the content pipeline (W1.3) and holds it to the
// repository; this page holds no fact of its own.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro'
import HomeSlider from '../components/HomeSlider.astro'
import HomeInstall from '../components/HomeInstall.astro'
---

<Base title="Fugaro">
  {/* Three top-level blocks, each carrying its own gutter and its own room below: `main:has(>
      .hero)` drops `main`'s padding on this page, so no block adds a top padding on top of the
      block above's bottom one, and the gap between two of them is one padding rather than two
      (`website/test/base-styles.mjs`'s `homeRhythmFailures` reads the three at 1280, 768 and
      375 px). */}
  <Hero />
  <HomeSlider />
  <HomeInstall />
</Base>
